# Implementation Plan - Phase G: Western Disturbance Reliability Specialist (Gate 6 / P1)

Phase G implements the **Western Disturbance Reliability Specialist (`WD_RELIABILITY_V1`)**, diagnosing medium-range NWP forecast failure for extratropical western disturbances affecting the Western Himalayas and Indo-Gangetic Plains without collapsing it into one opaque score. It explicitly decomposes western disturbance forecast reliability into:
1. **Arrival timing error** (arrival offset $> 6$ hours)
2. **Track/trough location error** (center/trough axis displacement $> 150$ km at 48h, $> 250$ km at 72h)
3. **Precipitation intensity error** (accumulated precipitation error $> 35$ mm/24h)
4. **Precipitation spatial displacement** (centroid misplacement $> 100$ km between orographic slope and plains)
5. **Event duration error** (system duration error $> 12$ hours)
6. **Rain/snow phase partition error** (strictly conditional on ground observation / freezing level availability; `null` when unsupported)
7. **Terrain-conditioned reliability** (explicitly separating Western Himalayan high altitude, foothill/sub-Himalayan, and Indo-Gangetic plain regimes)

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Decomposed Failure Modes**: Western Disturbance reliability will NOT be collapsed into one opaque score. Arrival timing, trough position, precipitation amount, spatial displacement, duration, and rain/snow partition are independently evaluated and reported.
> - **Rain/Snow Null Safety**: As required by the Phase G failure and rollback rules (*"Do not infer rain/snow failure without suitable observations"*), rain/snow phase partition is strictly `null` unless high-altitude observations and freezing level / surface temperature are explicitly present.
> - **Anti-Leakage & Issue-Time Boundary**: At issue time $t_0$, only $t_0$ features (subtropical jet speed/displacement, 500-hPa trough depth/tilt, induced low status, ensemble trough/precip spread, terrain class) enter inference. Ground truth observations (IMD/NCMRWF/snow-gauges) are sealed with 24h verification latency.

