### 2. Specialist Engine & Baseline Ladder

#### [NEW] [western_disturbance_specialist.py](file:///c:/Users/adity/OneDrive/Desktop/SIH26079-RII/backend/app/builder2/western_disturbance_specialist.py)
- `WesternDisturbanceReliabilitySpecialist`:
  - Implements the baseline ladder:
    1. Historical terrain-conditioned climatology baseline
    2. Raw ensemble trough spread baseline
    3. Spread-to-bust logistic regression
    4. Specialist (`WD_RELIABILITY_V1`) incorporating jet dynamics, 500 hPa trough depth, induced low, and terrain conditioning
    5. Terrain-conditioned conformal bounds (Western Himalayas vs Plains)
  - Decomposed predictors for:
    - Arrival timing failure ($> 6$h error)
    - Trough/center position failure ($> 150$ km error)
    - Precipitation amount failure ($> 35$ mm/24h error)
    - Precipitation spatial displacement ($> 100$ km error)
    - Event duration failure ($> 12$h error)
    - Rain/snow partition failure (strictly `null` unless observations and freezing level are present)
  - Out-of-Distribution (OOD) detection: extreme jet speed ($> 95$ m/s), extreme trough spread ($> 280$ km), or unprecedented negative tilt.
  - Conversion to universal `ReliabilityState` with continuous error distribution, monotonic survival curves, hazard curves, and terrain-conditioned failure motifs.

